---
description: "FastAPI backend rules (routing, dependencies, service boundaries)"
globs:
  - "**/*fastapi*.py"
  - "**/api/**/*.py"
  - "**/routers/**/*.py"
  - "**/endpoints/**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

# FastAPI Rules
- Keep route handlers thin: validate input, call service/use-case, map output.
- Move business logic to service/use-case layers.
- Use dependency injection for external boundaries (database, HTTP clients, queues).
- Return consistent HTTP errors and response shapes.
- Keep startup/config wiring separate from domain logic.
